  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (0.520) clearly outperforms pca_n2000 (0.485) for single-profile RNA, and image-only (resnet50) is very weak (0.208), suggesting RNA is the dominant signal. The multiprofile design axis is completely untested. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles (with simple avgpool) improve upon the best single-profile RNA result (config_004, scvi_n200, 0.520)? This isolates the multiprofile effect using the strongest encoder identified so far and the simplest aggregation, avoiding confounds from transformer aggregation or a weaker encoder. Why best next: Multiprofile is the largest untested structural axis; resolving whether it adds value (or not) with a clean, minimal change from config_004 will either open a promising direction for further exploitation (aggregation type, fusion) or allow us to deprioritize it and focus budget on encoder improvements or multimodal fusion."
}

